From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: amdv: hold the DV VSIF across disc-session source gaps

At every decoder swap inside a BD disc session (menu->title, segment
chains) the no-source gap makes the output policy momentarily leave
DOVI, and send_hdmi_pkt() tears the Dolby VSIF down to SDR. The sink
then does a full DV->SDR->DV re-lock (measured 3.2s VSIF gap plus TV
lock time) exactly as the next segment starts presenting - the viewer
loses the first seconds of every title (Superman: the first GOP of the
movie) and sees an SDR-decoded flash of the last DV frame.

Add dolby_vision_vsif_hold: while userspace holds it (the disc player
keeps every session segment in DV output by construction), swallow the
DOVI->SDR teardown so the VSIF stays latched and the next segment
resumes packet-identical - no HDMI transition at all. The holder
clears it at session end, releasing the normal SDR transition.

--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c	2026-07-20 16:59:53.774595913 -0400
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c	2026-07-20 17:00:27.273151760 -0400
@@ -174,6 +174,20 @@
 module_param(dolby_vision_enable, bool, 0664);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(dolby_vision_enable, "\n dolby_vision_enable\n");
 
+/* Disc-session VSIF hold: set by userspace while a disc player keeps every
+ * segment of a session in DV output (menus VS10-mapped, features native).
+ * While held, the DOVI->SDR HDMI packet teardown in send_hdmi_pkt() is
+ * suppressed so the short no-source gap at a segment/decoder swap never
+ * drops the Dolby VSIF: the sink stays DV-locked and the next segment
+ * resumes packet-identical, with no HDMI transition (no SDR flash, no
+ * multi-second DV re-lock swallowing the segment start). The holder must
+ * clear the flag at session end so the normal SDR transition can run.
+ */
+static bool dolby_vision_vsif_hold;
+static bool vsif_hold_active;
+module_param(dolby_vision_vsif_hold, bool, 0664);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dolby_vision_vsif_hold, "\n dolby_vision_vsif_hold\n");
+
 static bool amdv_efuse_bypass;
 module_param(amdv_efuse_bypass, bool, 0664);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(amdv_efuse_bypass, "\n amdv_efuse_bypass\n");
@@ -7257,6 +7271,7 @@
 		last_dst_format = dst_format;
 		vd_signal.signal_type = SIGNAL_DOVI;
 		notify_vd_signal_to_amvideo(&vd_signal);
+		vsif_hold_active = false;
 	} else if (last_dst_format != dst_format) {
 		if (last_dst_format == FORMAT_HDR10) {
 			sdr_transition_delay = 0;
@@ -7291,6 +7306,22 @@
 				}
 			}
 		} else if (last_dst_format == FORMAT_DOVI) {
+			if (dolby_vision_vsif_hold) {
+				/* segment swap inside a held disc session:
+				 * keep the DV VSIF latched and swallow the
+				 * transition. last_dst_format stays DOVI so
+				 * the next DV segment resumes with an
+				 * unchanged packet state (no transition at
+				 * the sink at all).
+				 */
+				if (!vsif_hold_active) {
+					vsif_hold_active = true;
+					pr_dv_dbg("send pkt: VSIF held across source gap (disc session)\n");
+				}
+				sdr_transition_delay = 0;
+				dolby_vision_flags &= ~FLAG_FORCE_HDMI_PKT;
+				return flag;
+			}
 			if (vinfo && vinfo->vout_device &&
 				vinfo->vout_device->fresh_tx_vsif_pkt) {
 				if (vf && (is_hlg_frame(vf) ||
